  "EMG-002": { en: "These may be signs of a stroke. Check the face: has it dropped on one side? Check the arms: can both be raised? Check the speech: is it slurred or strange? If you see any of these, time matters. Call one one two or go to the nearest hospital emergency department now. Note the time the signs started." },
  "EMG-003": { en: "Chest pain or pressure that lasts more than a few minutes, especially with sweating, breathlessness or pain spreading to the arm, jaw or back, can be a heart attack. Call one one two or go to the nearest hospital emergency department now. Sit down and rest while you wait. Do not drive yourself." },
  "EMG-004": { en: "Your blood sugar is low. If you can swallow safely, take something sugary now, such as half a bottle of a regular soft drink or three teaspoons of sugar in water. Check your sugar again in fifteen minutes. If it is still low, take sugar again. If you become drowsy or confused, someone should call one one two." },
  "EMG-005": { en: "Your blood sugar is very high. If you are vomiting, very thirsty, breathing fast, drowsy or confused, go to the nearest hospital emergency department now or call one one two. Keep drinking water if you can." },
  "EMG-006": { en: "If someone is having a seizure, keep them safe. Move hard objects away and put something soft under their head. Do not hold them down and do not put anything in their mouth. When the shaking stops, turn them onto their side. Call one one two if the seizure lasts more than five minutes, if it is their first seizure, or if they are hurt or pregnant." },
  "EMG-007": { en: "If you are struggling to breathe, cannot finish a sentence, or your lips are turning grey or blue, call one one two or go to the nearest hospital emergency department now. If you have a reliever inhaler, use it as your clinician showed you while you get help." },
  "EMG-008": { en: "In pregnancy, go to hospital straight away if you have bleeding from the vagina, a severe headache or blurred vision, fits, severe pain in your belly, fever, your waters breaking early, or your baby moving less than usual. Do not wait. Call one one two or go now." },
  "EMG-009": { en: "Take your child to hospital straight away if they cannot drink or breastfeed, are vomiting everything, have had a fit, are very sleepy or hard to wake, are breathing fast or with difficulty, or are a young baby with a fever. Do not wait." },
